  "updated": "2026-11-24",
  "intro": "Monarch, YNAB, Simplifi, Tiller and EveryDollar are five Copilot Money alternatives with published pricing and distinct budgeting methods. Published prices run from a free EveryDollar tier to $17.99 a month on EveryDollar Premium monthly billing, and each option differs in platform availability, trial duration and sharing rules. At The Modern Wallet, we compare published subscription costs and feature limits so households can assess their software expenses before paying.\n\n[Copilot Money](https://www.copilot.money) charges $9 per month, or $109 billed yearly as a limited-time offer down from $119. Copilot Money provides one plan with no tiers, no add-ons and no Artificial Intelligence (AI) credits, covering connections to over 16,000 banks, a money assistant and customer support from real humans. Its pricing page lists access for iPhone, iPad, Mac and Web, while its Households sharing feature is marked as coming soon.\n\nFor context on the broader market, explore our [best budgeting apps roundup](/roundup/best-budgeting-apps/) and our [best net worth tracker roundup](/roundup/best-net-worth-tracker/). If you want to evaluate specific competing products in depth, read our [Monarch alternatives](/alternatives/monarch-money/) guide, our [YNAB alternatives](/alternatives/ynab/) breakdown, or our [guide to making a budget](/guides/how-to-make-a-budget/).",
