  "stillBetterFit": {
    "heading": "When Copilot Money Is Still the Better Fit",
    "body": "Copilot Money remains the stronger choice for individuals on Apple devices or the Web who want a straightforward, single-tier subscription without upsells or feature tiers. Copilot Money charges $9 per month or $109 billed yearly, providing access to all features with no tiers, no add-ons, and no AI credits.\n\nCopilot Money connects to over 16,000 financial institutions, includes an interactive money assistant, and provides customer support from real humans. Its pricing page specifies access across iPhone, iPad, Mac and Web, making it practical for users within the Apple ecosystem who switch between desktop and mobile devices. Copilot Money also explicitly states that it never sells customer financial data.\n\nFor solo users who prefer an integrated money assistant over manual zero-based envelope calculations, Copilot Money offers a low monthly entry price of $9. Paying $9 each month totals $108 across 12 months, which is $71.88 less per year than paying monthly for Monarch Core ($179.88), YNAB ($179.88), or EveryDollar Premium ($215.88). If you do not need immediate multi-user sharing and prefer modern automated tracking on Apple hardware, Copilot Money provides that exact environment."
